import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a5 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Member credit implementation plan","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/subscription-billing/member-credit/plan.md","filePath":"feature/subscription-billing/member-credit/plan.md"}'),o={name:"feature/subscription-billing/member-credit/plan.md"};function r(s,e,c,d,l,p){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="member-credit-implementation-plan" tabindex="-1">Member credit implementation plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#member-credit-implementation-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Member credit implementation plan&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="ai-integration-slice-—-2026-10-20" tabindex="-1">AI integration slice — 2026-10-20 <a class="header-anchor" href="#ai-integration-slice-—-2026-10-20" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;AI integration slice — 2026-10-20&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Rollout: 20/10 AI-execution delta, then DEV_SEED-source delta, then optional guarded local Demo seed. Init includes both schema changes, never the dev seed. Balance adds developmentAvailable without reclassifying it as a purchase. Existing headers X-Workspace-Id are overwritten by Gateway; callers must use X-AI-Workspace-Id + Idempotency-Key. Other clients (e.g. mobile) must adopt this contract before invoking generation. Video status GET has a 15-second timeout and its own private scheduler so existing mail/publishing schedules are unaffected. The dev-only monthly anchor is provisional test setup; later verified subscription provisioning needs an explicit anchor transition review, not silently inferred payment.</p><p>Additionally apply the existing verify_internal_key dependency to the AI hashtag endpoint, matching other generation routes. No provider, prompt, editor, publishing or content-writing redesign. Verify authentication dependency without live provider invocation.</p><p>Add a delta and matching init reservation dispatch state, cached JSON response and unique video job ID. JDBC execution store + orchestration service + bounded scheduled video reconciliation. Reserve/finalize in short committed transactions, no DB transaction across provider I/O. Replace AI proxy calls only; retain response bodies/routes. Canonical enriched JSON SHA-256 fingerprint, CAS dispatch claim, no blind redispatch. Web shared helper adds Workspace header/per-action UUID, translates errors, invalidates scoped reports; narrow Editor error handling. Verify with isolated PostgreSQL/fake upstream, compilation/typecheck/lint; no paid provider call. Seed only exact confirmed local Agency, no fake payment rows.</p><p>&gt; Local rollout 2026-10-20: both revised Credit migrations have now been applied and postchecked on <code>brandhub-postgres</code> / <code>brandhub.public</code> at the user&#39;s request, without seeding or legacy conversion. See <a href="./manual-test.html">manual-test.md</a> for the role-based test guide and expected account-not-ready state. Earlier no-APPLY statements below are historical; no Mongo/Atlas change was made.</p><h2 id="web-reporting-implementation-—-2026-10-20" tabindex="-1">Web reporting implementation — 2026-10-20 <a class="header-anchor" href="#web-reporting-implementation-—-2026-10-20" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Web reporting implementation — 2026-10-20&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Extend <code>src/pages/credit/types/credit.ts</code> and <code>services/creditService.ts</code> with balance, own limit and own/member usage. Shared Axios only, AbortSignal on Credit reads, integer safety on displayed/derived amounts. Add feature query-key/options helpers and separate context/reporting hooks; keep existing optimistic-revision API contracts.</li><li>Thin <code>index.tsx</code> resolves URL Agency with authenticated-user-scoped query, then renders Owner or personal components. Open the Credit access rule to Owner/Manager/Creator; existing Agency sidebar entry follows it. Owner controls are gated by actual Agency ownerId, not a Workspace role. No AuthGuard/global theme redesign.</li><li>Add balance summary, usage report, personal view and read-only catalog components. Reuse CreditQueryState/AmountForm; selected member panel combines existing limit form with usage and searchable one-click member selection. Independent reads run in parallel. No all-member usage fan-out, provider calls, polling, aggregate Agency spending or historical UI.</li><li>Keep Admin operation picker/editor; add explicit units and compact integration disclosure using existing HelpHint. Forms validate on blur and submit, reload uses actual returned saved values (including same revision). Do not auto-save monetary policy on every keypress. Invalidate relevant reports after writes without resetting unrelated drafts.</li><li>Update both <code>src/i18n/locales/vi/credit.json</code> and <code>en/credit.json</code>. Scoped ESLint/Prettier, TypeScript and production bundle; Playwright CLI with API fixtures for permissions, races/cache switching, errors and themes/responsiveness. Temporary artifacts only in ignored output/playwright, no tests under src. No real DB writes or migration APPLY.</li></ol><p>Status: Web reporting/configuration slice implemented and fixture verified (42 main + 19 additional assertions). Open Credit from the selected Agency menu at <code>/agency/:id/credit</code>; Admin pricing is <code>/admin/credit-prices</code>. To test with live services, first review/apply the revised 19/10 then 20/10 migrations to an appropriate DB and run the matching Business build. A former eight-table DB needs reviewed conversion; do not init it. Without verified grants/anchor, usage shows the prerequisite state. The Web has no manual funding or buy-credit action. AI and payment integration remains separate work.</p><p>&gt; Compact revision: <a href="./compact-schema.html">compact-schema.md</a> supersedes references below to separate policy, member-limit, account and usage tables. Revised 19/10 and 20/10 deltas, init and Business Credit stores now use the compact baseline; 54 accounting, 41 configuration and 25 MVC checks passed on that schema. Public API contracts are unchanged; no shared DB APPLY or AI/payment integration is implied.</p><h2 id="accounting-handoff-and-setup-—-2026-10-20" tabindex="-1">Accounting handoff and setup — 2026-10-20 <a class="header-anchor" href="#accounting-handoff-and-setup-—-2026-10-20" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Accounting handoff and setup — 2026-10-20&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Existing DB: review configuration delta 2026-10-19, then accounting delta 2026-10-20; use <code>psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f &lt;reviewed-file&gt;</code>. Both contain transactions. Fresh DB uses current init only. Mongo is unchanged. No shared DB has been upgraded during this implementation.</li><li>Implemented: atomic reserve/settle/release, locked price, Plan-first allocation, member ceiling, persistent purchased grants, anchored monthly usage and read reporting. Read routes under <code>/api/v1/agencies/{agencyId}/credit</code>: Owner <code>GET /balance</code>, member <code>GET /usage/me</code>, Owner <code>GET /members/{memberId}/usage</code>. Reports include only new accounting records, not legacy aggregates.</li><li>Server-only <code>CreditGrantService.applyPlan(agencyId, subscriptionId, paymentId)</code> reads plan quota from DB. Paid plans require completed paid transaction owned by Agency Owner, <code>PLAN:&lt;planName&gt;</code> reference and payment time within entitlement period. ACTIVE alone is not payment proof. Free plans need no paid transaction.</li><li>Server-only <code>applyPurchase(agencyId, paymentId)</code> verifies completed BUY_CREDIT payment, positive paid amount and trusted <code>CREDIT:&lt;quantity&gt;</code> order reference. Payment code must construct that reference server-side. Never accept browser-supplied grant quantities. Invoke handoffs within the verified PostgreSQL payment/subscription transaction; no public grant endpoint exists.</li><li>Grants cannot duplicate a transaction across Agencies or issue two full Plan quotas for the same Agency period. Original monthly anchor stays fixed. Monthly aligned periods are supported; annual periods, mid-period upgrade/proration and cross-Agency allocation require separate integration, not an invented full-quota regrant.</li><li>Pending: AI endpoint adapters, durable dispatch/job ownership and result replay, unknown-outcome reconciliation and Payment/Subscription hook calls. Member tracking UI is now implemented in the Web reporting slice above. Returning the same reservation ID does NOT authorize dispatching another provider request. Do not advertise AI financial enforcement before end-to-end integration checks.</li><li>Unknown outcomes stay RESERVED for reconciliation. Server-only settlement uses successful units and original period/price; no automatic timeout refund. Owner bypasses personal ceiling only, never shared balance.</li></ul><h2 id="accounting-implementation-—-2026-10-20" tabindex="-1">Accounting implementation — 2026-10-20 <a class="header-anchor" href="#accounting-implementation-—-2026-10-20" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Accounting implementation — 2026-10-20&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Implement confirmed fallback 10, request/output units and anchored monthly continuation first. Add <code>CreditCycle</code> pure calendar utility, additive accounting migration/init, JDBC accounting store and transactional accounting service. Add server-only grant handoff contract (not exposed as a browser API), exact integer arithmetic, Agency account serialization, per-period member usage and reservation allocations with locked price revisions. Legacy aggregates are not overwritten. Test insufficient funds/member limits, concurrency, duplicate keys, partial success, expired Plan credits, old-cycle completion and purchased persistence on isolated PostgreSQL before connecting generation adapters. No grant or real provider invocation is run during tests. UI/reporting and AI orchestration must not be claimed complete by accounting core alone.</p><ol><li>Configuration foundation: additive <code>ai_credit_policies</code>, <code>ai_credit_member_limits</code>, <code>ai_credit_operation_prices</code>. Retain legacy tables and consumers. Policy and overrides use optimistic revisions; immutable price rows keyed by operation/revision. Admin pricing serialized per operation with a PostgreSQL transaction advisory lock. Foreign keys restrict accidental deletion of audit history.</li><li>Business native SQL store for guarded configuration writes (matching existing JDBC stores); service-level tenant/user authorization, transactional writes, DTO records and thin controllers. Explicit Admin check even if called outside route security. No startup schema mutation or external calls.</li><li>After product decisions: design shared balance ownership and subscription-period grants, member usage and durable reservations. Define Payment-owned top-up contract and prevent repeat grants. Unknown completion stays held pending reconciliation; no unsafe timeout refund.</li><li>Integrate synchronous content first, then asynchronous image/video with explicit request IDs and per-unit completion, no blanket proxy interception or new charge on polling/reuse. Identify every billable route before enabling enforcement.</li><li>Owner/member UI and Admin price editor. Follow Web rules, feature-local hooks/services/types, parallel vi/en <code>credit</code> locale namespace, existing light/dark design. No changes to publish/Task approval/Yjs.</li><li>Isolated SQL/API/browser tests, migration instructions and staged rollout. Never run init on existing DB or apply shared DB changes without operator authorization. No test source files committed per user instruction; temporary checks live under ignored target/output only.</li></ol><p>No PayOS implementation, manual seed credit, fabricated price, automatic legacy aggregate backfill, shared DB APPLY, commit or push in this scope.</p><h2 id="configuration-ui-implementation" tabindex="-1">Configuration UI implementation <a class="header-anchor" href="#configuration-ui-implementation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Configuration UI implementation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Feature <code>brandhub-web/src/pages/credit/</code>: types, service using shared Axios, hooks using TanStack Query, amount form, policy/member panels, and Admin price panel. Thin <code>index.tsx</code> and <code>prices.tsx</code> route pages. Reuse Agency listMembers service; lazy-load routes and extend only Credit-specific navigation/access entries. Locales: <code>src/i18n/locales/{vi,en}/credit.json</code>, registered in existing i18n index. No dependencies or design system generation; existing BrandHub system is authoritative. Background focus refresh disabled while editing; errors preserve text, revision conflicts require explicit reload. Test browser with intercepted API only, no live configuration writes.</p><h2 id="setup-for-the-configuration-slice" tabindex="-1">Setup for the configuration slice <a class="header-anchor" href="#setup-for-the-configuration-slice" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Setup for the configuration slice&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Existing PostgreSQL: review and run only <code>docs/database/migrations/2026-10-19-member-credit-configuration.sql</code> against the intended database with <code>psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f ...</code>. The script contains its own transaction. Do not run init or archived migrations on existing data. No database has been upgraded by this code change.</li><li>Fresh PostgreSQL: current <code>init-postgres-v2.sql</code> already creates the same tables; no separate delta replay is needed. Mongo is unchanged.</li><li>Compile/restart Business. Missing configuration tables return <code>503 CREDIT_SCHEMA_NOT_READY</code> on the new APIs, not automatic schema creation. Existing AI/Billing flows are untouched.</li><li>Owner first GETs <code>/api/v1/agencies/{agencyId}/credit/policy</code>; if missing it returns <code>defaultMemberLimit: null, revision: 0</code>. PUT with <code>{ &quot;defaultMemberLimit&quot;: &lt;owner-selected amount&gt;, &quot;expectedRevision&quot;: 0 }</code>. Zero is valid, not unlimited. No invented initial amount.</li><li>Owner GETs <code>/api/v1/agencies/{agencyId}/credit/members/{userId}/limit</code> to obtain override revision. PUT the same path with <code>{ &quot;memberLimit&quot;: &lt;chosen amount&gt;, &quot;expectedRevision&quot;: &lt;returned revision&gt; }</code>. No override resolves the current Agency default, then system fallback 10 (<code>SYSTEM_DEFAULT</code>); this is a ceiling, not a join-time credit grant. Existing legacy creator limits are not automatically imported.</li><li>Authenticated users GET <code>/api/v1/credit/prices</code>; empty means no configured prices, never free AI. Admin PUTs <code>/api/v1/admin/credit/prices/CONTENT_GENERATE</code> with <code>{ &quot;unitCredits&quot;: &lt;admin-selected price&gt;, &quot;enabled&quot;: true, &quot;expectedRevision&quot;: 0 }</code>. Subsequent edits use the returned revision. Content/caption/hashtag units are successful requests; image/video units are successful outputs. Generation adapters remain pending; the example image price 3 is not a configured product price.</li><li>These APIs configure policy only. They do not make AI chargeable yet, allocate Plan credit or complete FR 3.9.5 reporting. Do not advertise financial enforcement until the remaining checklist passes and Subscription supplies authoritative Agency grants. The existing Subscription subscribe endpoint currently activates without verified payment; do not use that as proof of a paid credit grant.</li></ol>',20)])])}const g=i(o,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
